      "year": 2011,
      "abstract": "Value-driven design is a movement that is using economic theory to transform systems engineering to better use optimization to improve the design of large systems, particularly in aerospace and defense. This paper describes the ideas and methods that are current in value-driven design. An overview of the history of value-driven design is provided, leading up to a survey of the approaches and techniques that are currently being studied and implemented in university research and experimental government programs. The paper closes with a discussion of the potential benefits that may be realized by employing the value-driven design framework. Copyright © 2010 by Value-Driven Design Institute.",
